00:39:58,030 --> 00:39:58,863
- [Tom] Hmm.

1019
00:39:58,863 --> 00:40:00,032
I see.

1020
00:40:00,032 --> 00:40:00,867
(metal pinging)

1021
00:40:00,867 --> 00:40:01,767
- [Tom] Oh, dammit.

1022
00:40:01,767 --> 00:40:03,002
Radiator.

1023
00:40:03,002 --> 00:40:05,537
- Wow, John Cage
on the soundtrack.

1024
00:40:07,907 --> 00:40:09,708
- [Tom] Oh, criminy,
they're closed.

1025
00:40:09,708 --> 00:40:10,542
(light synth music)

1026
00:40:10,542 --> 00:40:11,477
Hmm?

1027
00:40:11,477 --> 00:40:12,612
- [Mike] Oh, no.

1028
00:40:12,612 --> 00:40:13,412
No.

1029
00:40:13,412 --> 00:40:15,147
- [Tom] Oh, boy.

1030
00:40:15,147 --> 00:40:17,750
- [Mike] Oh, he put on a skort.

1031
00:40:21,053 --> 00:40:23,188
- [Tom] I beg you
to think this over.

1032
00:40:23,188 --> 00:40:24,022
- Turn back.

1033
00:40:24,022 --> 00:40:24,857
- [Mike] No.

1034
00:40:24,857 --> 00:40:25,690
It's not too late.

1035
00:40:25,690 --> 00:40:26,525
- [Tom] Oh.

1036
00:40:26,525 --> 00:40:27,358
No, no, no, no.

1037
00:40:27,358 --> 00:40:28,360
- No.

1038
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:30,328
- He's wearing jockey for her!

1039
00:40:30,328 --> 00:40:31,163
Ah!

1040
00:40:32,965 --> 00:40:34,733
- [Tom] You're supposed
to shower first!

1041
00:40:34,733 --> 00:40:36,435
- Or at least rinse
out your jockeys.

1042
00:40:36,435 --> 00:40:37,302
Ew.

1043
00:40:37,302 --> 00:40:38,670
- [Mike] Ew.

1044
00:40:38,670 --> 00:40:40,605
- [Tom] Fungus and thing.

1045
00:40:40,605 --> 00:40:42,407
- Oh, and he's sucking
up bathtub water!

1046
00:40:42,407 --> 00:40:43,242
Oh!

1047
00:40:43,242 --> 00:40:45,277
(metal scraping)

1048
00:40:45,277 --> 00:40:48,113
- I know my locker's around
here somewhere, now where?

1049
00:40:48,113 --> 00:40:49,248
Is it that one?

1050
00:40:49,248 --> 00:40:52,752
(light synth music)

1051
00:40:52,752 --> 00:40:54,085
- [Mike] Enya.

1052
00:40:54,085 --> 00:40:55,287
Sorry, got a cramp.

1053
00:40:55,287 --> 00:40:56,488
I can't get up.

1054
00:40:58,090 --> 00:41:02,393
- Can we turn on the
fuzzy bubbles, please?

1055
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:03,862
- [Tom] God, he's touching me.

1056
00:41:03,862 --> 00:41:08,100
I specifically have no-touch
clause in my contract.

1057
00:41:09,100 --> 00:41:09,935
(laughs)

1058
00:41:09,935 --> 00:41:10,903
(metal clanging)

1059
00:41:10,903 --> 00:41:12,137
- What was that?

1060
00:41:12,137 --> 00:41:13,505
- What was what?

1061
00:41:13,505 --> 00:41:15,473
- I thought I heard
something in the locker room.

1062
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:16,475
- Oh, come on.

1063
00:41:16,475 --> 00:41:17,943
There's nobody here.

1064
00:41:17,943 --> 00:41:18,977
It's probably just old Joe
trying to sneak a peek of you.

1065
00:41:18,977 --> 00:41:20,578
He's a horny old guy.

1066
00:41:20,578 --> 00:41:22,080
- Oh, please, just
for me, just go see.

1067
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:23,982
I swear to God I
heard something.

1068
00:41:23,982 --> 00:41:25,283
- There's nobody else here.

1069
00:41:25,283 --> 00:41:26,452
The place is locked up.

1070
00:41:26,452 --> 00:41:27,720
- Please.

1071
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:28,953
- [Tom] Hey, she's got
her hair on sideways.

1072
00:41:28,953 --> 00:41:31,490
- There was a noise,
I'm telling please go.

1073
00:41:31,490 --> 00:41:32,323
- All right.

1074
00:41:32,323 --> 00:41:33,825
(wretches)

1075
00:41:33,825 --> 00:41:36,262
- [Mike] Oh, he just had
to get that in, didn't he.

1076
00:41:36,262 --> 00:41:37,095
- [Tom] No, no, no!

1077
00:41:37,095 --> 00:41:38,097
- [Mike] No!

1078
00:41:38,963 --> 00:41:41,400
(shouting)

1079
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:42,868
- [Tom] Hate that.

1080
00:41:42,868 --> 00:41:44,703
- See, look, I told you,
there's nobody here.

1081
00:41:44,703 --> 00:41:46,038
(roars)

1082
00:41:46,038 --> 00:41:47,607
(screams)

1083
00:41:47,607 --> 00:41:49,842
- [Tom] Oh, zombie chiropractor.

1084
00:41:49,842 --> 00:41:51,477
Oh, thank you.

1085
00:41:51,477 --> 00:41:52,745
- [Mike] Pool cleaner, ma'am.

1086
00:41:52,745 --> 00:41:55,280
pH check and I'll
be out of your way.

1087
00:41:55,280 --> 00:41:57,817
(water splashing)

1088
00:41:57,817 --> 00:41:58,850
There goes a great
tennis player.

1089
00:41:58,850 --> 00:42:00,987
(growls)

1090
00:42:00,987 --> 00:42:01,720
- [Tom] Wedgie!

1091
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:04,357
(screams)

1092
00:42:04,357 --> 00:42:08,993
- [Mike] Oh, excuse me, but
the dead don't tread water.

1093
00:42:08,993 --> 00:42:12,097
- [Tom] George Romero's
"Casey at the Bat."

1094
00:42:12,097 --> 00:42:14,500
(screams)

1095
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:18,403
- She must have studied
under Jamie Lee Curtis.

1096
00:42:19,472 --> 00:42:21,640
(screams)

1097
00:42:25,277 --> 00:42:26,145
- [Mike] Eh, hang on.

1098
00:42:26,145 --> 00:42:26,978
Oh, my ankle.

1099
00:42:26,978 --> 00:42:27,813
Ow.

1100
00:42:27,813 --> 00:42:29,348
(screams)

1101
00:42:29,348 --> 00:42:31,717
- [Tom] "Grady,"
this fall on NBC.

1102
00:42:31,717 --> 00:42:32,585
- Hey, Fred.

1103
00:42:32,585 --> 00:42:33,818
- Look at that.

1104
00:42:39,892 --> 00:42:42,695
- [Tom] She's briskly
jogging from him.

1105
00:42:42,695 --> 00:42:44,297
- [Mike] You know, he did
kill that creep for her.

1106
00:42:44,297 --> 00:42:47,132
She could thank him, at least.

1107
00:42:47,132 --> 00:42:51,803
- [Tom] Hey, it's your
typical free week at the Y.

1108
00:42:51,803 --> 00:42:55,673
- Hey, come on back and
shag some flies for me.

1109
00:42:57,610 --> 00:42:59,912
- [Mike] Don't use the exit.

1110
00:43:01,147 --> 00:43:04,248
- Come on, we need a
short center fielder.

1111
00:43:06,885 --> 00:43:10,755
- [Tom] Oh, zombie
never could hit a curve.

1112
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:12,758
- [Mike] You know, John
Goodman on Hume Cronin's back

1113
00:43:12,758 --> 00:43:14,593
could outrun this guy.

1114
00:43:18,130 --> 00:43:20,065
- Oh, no, her bra strap broke.

1115
00:43:20,065 --> 00:43:21,533
- [Tom] What next?

1116
00:43:21,533 --> 00:43:22,702
(screams)

1117
00:43:22,702 --> 00:43:26,072
- Okay, okay, I'm
giving you a head start.

1118
00:43:28,907 --> 00:43:30,608
♪ Woke up, fell out of bed ♪

1119
00:43:30,608 --> 00:43:32,310
♪ Dragged the comb
across my head ♪

1120
00:43:32,310 --> 00:43:33,578
♪ Found my way down the stairs ♪

1121
00:43:33,578 --> 00:43:34,413
- [Crow] What's going to happen?

1122
00:43:34,413 --> 00:43:35,247
I, oh.

1123
00:43:41,287 --> 00:43:44,323
(upbeat synth music)

1124
00:43:47,292 --> 00:43:51,963
♪ Touchdown in the land
of the Delta blues ♪

1125
00:43:51,963 --> 00:43:56,302
♪ In the middle of
the pouring rain ♪

1126
00:43:57,737 --> 00:43:58,937
- Oh, wonderful.

1127
00:43:58,937 --> 00:43:59,905
- Yeah.

1128
00:43:59,905 --> 00:44:02,307
- Hey, thanks for that back rub.

1129
00:44:02,307 --> 00:44:03,475
Water feels great.

1130
00:44:03,475 --> 00:44:05,343
- Yeah, hardly
feel those injuries

1131
00:44:05,343 --> 00:44:06,812
I sustained when
you ran me over.

1132
00:44:06,812 --> 00:44:08,080
(laughs)

1133
00:44:08,080 --> 00:44:10,682
- Let me just say, I
am totally relaxed.

1134
00:44:10,682 --> 00:44:12,283
(giggles)

1135
00:44:12,283 --> 00:44:13,252
- Servo, stop that!

1136
00:44:13,252 --> 00:44:14,085
(giggles)

1137
00:44:14,085 --> 00:44:14,920
- What?

1138
00:44:14,920 --> 00:44:15,753
What, Crow?

1139
00:44:15,753 --> 00:44:16,588
What?

1140
00:44:16,588 --> 00:44:17,522
Huh?

1141
00:44:17,522 --> 00:44:18,457
- Stop it, you nutty nut nut.

1142
00:44:18,457 --> 00:44:19,223
- Crow, I'm not doing anything.

1143
00:44:19,223 --> 00:44:20,225
(screaming)

1144
00:44:20,225 --> 00:44:22,127
(spitting)

1145
00:44:22,127 --> 00:44:22,995
- Hey, guys.

1146
00:44:22,995 --> 00:44:23,828
(screaming)

1147
00:44:23,828 --> 00:44:24,663
- Dinner?

1148
00:44:24,663 --> 00:44:25,963
(screaming)

1149
00:44:25,963 --> 00:44:28,633
(alarm blaring)

1150
00:44:41,480 --> 00:44:44,383
- [Tom] Where'd
you get the fish?

1151
00:44:44,383 --> 00:44:45,550
- [Mike] Hey, Conan O'Brien.

1152
00:44:45,550 --> 00:44:46,552
(camera shutter clicking)

1153
00:44:46,552 --> 00:44:48,987
- [All] We didn't do it.

1154
00:44:48,987 --> 00:44:51,090
- Another unruly crowd.

1155
00:44:51,090 --> 00:44:51,957
- [Man] Frank.

1156
00:44:51,957 --> 00:44:53,192
- Yeah?

1157
00:44:53,192 --> 00:44:54,158
- Forensic's just
about finished.

1158
00:44:54,158 --> 00:44:55,260
The ME wants to see you inside.

1159
00:44:55,260 --> 00:44:57,195
- [Mike] What did I do?

1160
00:44:58,463 --> 00:44:59,998
- Great.

1161
00:44:59,998 --> 00:45:02,567
- [Tom] Fine,
everybody dump on me.

1162
00:45:02,567 --> 00:45:07,572
- Look, uh, keep an eye on
my star witness here, okay?

1163
00:45:08,440 --> 00:45:09,742
- Say, officer, can I go now?

1164
00:45:09,742 --> 00:45:10,742
- [Frank] Uh, soon.

1165
00:45:10,742 --> 00:45:12,143
I've got a few more questions.

1166
00:45:12,143 --> 00:45:14,647
- Can I have a Tahitian treat?

1167
00:45:15,513 --> 00:45:16,948
- [Tom] Poor guy.

1168
00:45:18,383 --> 00:45:19,217
Hmm.

1169
00:45:20,918 --> 00:45:22,453
- [Mike] Yep, yep, this
is the scene they always

1170
00:45:22,453 --> 00:45:24,823
show on "That's Hollywood,"
with Tom Bosley.

1171
00:45:24,823 --> 00:45:25,657
- [Tom] Beautiful.

1172
00:45:25,657 --> 00:45:27,025
Beautiful.

1173
00:45:27,025 --> 00:45:27,960
- [Mike] That's Bosley.

1174
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:29,193
(camera shutter clicking)

1175
00:45:29,193 --> 00:45:30,395
- Now let's get one
of you with the body.

1176
00:45:30,395 --> 00:45:32,097
- Wishful thinking, doc?

1177
00:45:32,097 --> 00:45:33,498
- Ah, Frank.

1178
00:45:33,498 --> 00:45:36,668
Nice to see you could
make it to the clambake.

1179
00:45:36,668 --> 00:45:39,772
- [Tom] Are you
talking to the Penguin?

1180
00:45:39,772 --> 00:45:41,273
- Oh, what the hell Else?

1181
00:45:41,273 --> 00:45:42,073
would I be doing at three
o'clock in the morning?

1182
00:45:42,073 --> 00:45:43,342
- I don't want to know.

1183
00:45:43,342 --> 00:45:44,610
- See your boys in white
are moving right along.

1184
00:45:44,610 --> 00:45:46,578
- Well, you've probably
noticed the lovely lady

1185
00:45:46,578 --> 00:45:47,813
on her way out.

1186
00:45:48,947 --> 00:45:51,048
Now the boys are trying
to fish lover-boy

1187
00:45:51,048 --> 00:45:53,552
out of the swimming
pool full of blood.

1188
00:45:53,552 --> 00:45:55,120
- [Mike] Uh, about your voice.

1189
00:45:55,120 --> 00:45:57,288
- You get anything out
of the good old Joe?

1190
00:45:57,288 --> 00:46:00,292
- Oh, old Joe is a wealth
of useful information.

1191
00:46:00,292 --> 00:46:01,293
- Yeah?

1192
00:46:01,293 --> 00:46:02,593
- Do you know how many times

1193
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:03,828
they refinish the
floors in here?

1194
00:46:03,828 --> 00:46:05,730
(laughs)

1195
00:46:05,730 --> 00:46:07,165
(laughs)

1196
00:46:07,165 --> 00:46:09,468
According to Joe, nobody
came in, no one could get in.

1197
00:46:09,468 --> 00:46:14,138
Now, bodies A and B stayed late
for a post-game celebration,

1198
00:46:14,138 --> 00:46:15,140
as was their habit.

1199
00:46:15,140 --> 00:46:16,675
- Yeah.

1200
00:46:16,675 --> 00:46:18,410
- Old Joe was sleeping like
a baby, never heard a thing.

1201
00:46:18,410 --> 00:46:19,377
- [Tom] So who put the
12-year-old in charge

1202
00:46:19,377 --> 00:46:21,147
of the investigation here?

1203
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:24,448
- So what do you
think, double suicide?

1204
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:25,283
- [Mike] No thanks.

1205
00:46:25,283 --> 00:46:26,818
- Oh, sure, sure.

1206
00:46:26,818 --> 00:46:31,088
Lover-boy smashes her head
in with the baseball bat,

1207
00:46:31,088 --> 00:46:35,493
then snaps his own neck
with his bare hands

1208
00:46:35,493 --> 00:46:38,663
and throws himself in
the pool out of remorse.

1209
00:46:38,663 --> 00:46:40,365
- [Tom] Well, you're the tailor.

1210
00:46:40,365 --> 00:46:41,733
- Bare hands?

1211
00:46:41,733 --> 00:46:43,268
- From the looks of it, yeah.

1212
00:46:43,268 --> 00:46:45,370
- Boy, police work
is really hard.

1213
00:46:45,370 --> 00:46:47,805
- So unless old Joe is
secretly pumping iron--

1214
00:46:47,805 --> 00:46:51,543
- You're looking for
one large, angry person.

1215
00:46:53,478 --> 00:46:55,413
- [Mike] Maybe I am looking
for someone like that,

1216
00:46:55,413 --> 00:46:58,483
but I don't think
I'll ever find him.

1217
00:47:03,688 --> 00:47:04,923
- [Tom] Don't touch me.

1218
00:47:04,923 --> 00:47:08,027
- I guess I'll need more
tape than I thought.

1219
00:47:08,027 --> 00:47:09,828
(rock music blaring)

1220
00:47:09,828 --> 00:47:10,995
- [Mike] Geez.

1221
00:47:12,330 --> 00:47:15,833
Maybe he should put the speakers
on the inside of his car.

1222
00:47:15,833 --> 00:47:19,605
- [Tom] Hey, threw meat
loaf at my mom today.

1223
00:47:21,005 --> 00:47:24,710
- I'm going to be involved
with a Sagittarius this week.

1224
00:47:24,710 --> 00:47:27,778
- Two teens overdose
on angel dust?

1225
00:47:27,778 --> 00:47:29,013
What?

1226
00:47:29,013 --> 00:47:30,515
- [Tom] What is up
with Mark Trail?

1227
00:47:30,515 --> 00:47:32,317
- Peter never did any dust, man.

1228
00:47:32,317 --> 00:47:34,252
- [Tom] He was a crack head.

1229
00:47:34,252 --> 00:47:35,753
- What's going on?

1230
00:47:35,753 --> 00:47:36,788
- Are they really dead?

1231
00:47:36,788 --> 00:47:37,722
I, I don't believe it's them.

1232
00:47:37,722 --> 00:47:38,890
There must be some mistake.

1233
00:47:38,890 --> 00:47:39,825
- Yeah.

1234
00:47:39,825 --> 00:47:41,693
yes, they're really dead.

1235
00:47:41,693 --> 00:47:44,128
- Where's our order?

1236
00:47:44,128 --> 00:47:46,698
- Man, what is so funny?

1237
00:47:46,698 --> 00:47:48,967
- [Mike] Did you see Russell
Baker's column this morning?

1238
00:47:48,967 --> 00:47:50,602
- It's great, man.

1239
00:47:50,602 --> 00:47:51,937
He killed them.

1240
00:47:51,937 --> 00:47:53,638
- What are you talking about?

1241
00:47:53,638 --> 00:47:56,408
- That big goon we
flattened the other night.

1242
00:47:56,408 --> 00:47:58,543
I guess we didn't finish
the job after all.

1243
00:47:58,543 --> 00:47:59,745
- Oh, my God.

1244
00:47:59,745 --> 00:48:00,678
- [Tom] Suddenly
the Twist and Creme

1245
00:48:00,678 --> 00:48:01,580
seemed a much darker place.

1246
00:48:01,580 --> 00:48:03,382
- Psycho might be right.

1247
00:48:03,382 --> 00:48:04,950
- I thought you said
no one knew it was us.

1248
00:48:04,950 --> 00:48:06,818
I thought you said
that no one saw us.

1249
00:48:06,818 --> 00:48:08,053
- Calm down.

1250
00:48:08,053 --> 00:48:09,755
- I'm sorry I was
thinking again.

1251
00:48:09,755 --> 00:48:11,423
- Just go in the car, all right?

1252
00:48:11,423 --> 00:48:12,757
I'll be with you in a minute.

1253
00:48:12,757 --> 00:48:13,992
- [Mike] Go to the car.

1254
00:48:13,992 --> 00:48:17,662
Bring your Dilly Bar
to the car, honey.

1255
00:48:17,662 --> 00:48:19,765
- [Tom] I should have
joined the PGA tour.

1256
00:48:19,765 --> 00:48:22,200
- [Jim] She's a
tough broad, man.

1257
00:48:22,200 --> 00:48:23,468
- Forget her.

1258
00:48:23,468 --> 00:48:25,603
What are we going to do
about our big friend?

1259
00:48:25,603 --> 00:48:27,672
- Or friends, man.

1260
00:48:27,672 --> 00:48:28,907
I say let 'em come.

1261
00:48:28,907 --> 00:48:30,575
- I'll throw pasta at 'em.

1262
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:32,510
- I, uh, just might
scalp me a few.

1263
00:48:32,510 --> 00:48:34,647
- Christ, man, put
that thing away.

1264
00:48:34,647 --> 00:48:37,548
Someone killed Peter and Susie.

1265
00:48:37,548 --> 00:48:38,750
This isn't a game.

1266
00:48:38,750 --> 00:48:40,252
- Lay off me, man.

1267
00:48:40,252 --> 00:48:41,787
- I just want you to chill out.

1268
00:48:41,787 --> 00:48:42,620
- No way.

1269
00:48:44,188 --> 00:48:45,423
- Why, Jimbo?

1270
00:48:45,423 --> 00:48:49,127
- [Mike] I'm Generation
X, that's why.

1271
00:48:49,127 --> 00:48:51,497
- Because I'm
having a good time.

1272
00:48:51,497 --> 00:48:55,533
- [Tom] Can't you just
support me in that, Phil?

1273
