00:57:53,905 --> 00:57:54,772
- Sorry, doc.

1526
00:57:54,772 --> 00:57:56,307
- For what?

1527
00:57:56,307 --> 00:57:59,243
The kid was a bum, he was
a disgrace to his family.

1528
00:57:59,243 --> 00:58:01,545
- [Mike] Yah, he goes
up with his sentences.

1529
00:58:01,545 --> 00:58:03,213
- Maybe he nailed
himself with a baseball,

1530
00:58:03,213 --> 00:58:04,548
you know what I mean.

1531
00:58:04,548 --> 00:58:08,052
- Yeah, I got it
drug-induced suicide.

1532
00:58:08,052 --> 00:58:11,655
- Hey, Frank, I believe
you're coming along.

1533
00:58:11,655 --> 00:58:13,323
- Thanks, doc.

1534
00:58:13,323 --> 00:58:16,327
- [Tom] So, should they just
leave him there, or not?

1535
00:58:16,327 --> 00:58:18,997
(ominous music)

1536
00:58:23,267 --> 00:58:26,003
- Why, it's a perfectly
good Peanut Buster Parfait.

1537
00:58:26,003 --> 00:58:27,005
- [Tom] Mmm.

1538
00:58:30,408 --> 00:58:32,910
- [Mike] Well, I wonder if this
knife's related to the case.

1539
00:58:32,910 --> 00:58:34,345
Nah, couldn't be.

1540
00:58:35,880 --> 00:58:38,650
- [Tom] I have no
idea what I'm doing.

1541
00:58:38,650 --> 00:58:40,285
When I get out of
my teens, I'm going

1542
00:58:40,285 --> 00:58:41,785
to be a great investigator.

1543
00:58:41,785 --> 00:58:43,120
(upbeat rock music)

1544
00:58:43,120 --> 00:58:44,955
(phone ringing)

1545
00:58:44,955 --> 00:58:49,960
♪ Slow ride ♪

1546
00:58:50,728 --> 00:58:53,297
♪ Stroke me, stroke me ♪

1547
00:58:53,297 --> 00:58:55,233
- Mod hair Ken bulks up.

1548
00:58:55,233 --> 00:58:58,402
(phone ringing)

1549
00:58:58,402 --> 00:59:00,438
- [Woman] Bobby, your
phone is ringing.

1550
00:59:00,438 --> 00:59:01,638
- Yeah, I can hear it, Ma.

1551
00:59:01,638 --> 00:59:03,608
(phone ringing)

1552
00:59:03,608 --> 00:59:07,745
- [Mike] Guy's got a real
Scott Thorson quality.

1553
00:59:07,745 --> 00:59:08,680
- [Woman] Get it, Bobby.

1554
00:59:08,680 --> 00:59:10,213
You've been in there a while.

1555
00:59:10,213 --> 00:59:13,852
- [Tom] Oh, it's probably
my chest grease supplier.

1556
00:59:13,852 --> 00:59:14,685
- Hello.

1557
00:59:14,685 --> 00:59:16,120
- Bob, this is Ames.

1558
00:59:16,120 --> 00:59:18,088
I just heard it on the radio,
What are we going to go?

1559
00:59:18,088 --> 00:59:19,457
- [Tom] U2 tickets are on sale.

1560
00:59:19,457 --> 00:59:20,358
- [Bobby] Amy, calm down.

1561
00:59:20,358 --> 00:59:21,192
What's wrong?

1562
00:59:21,192 --> 00:59:22,160
- What's wrong?

1563
00:59:22,160 --> 00:59:23,595
Jim's dead, Bob.

1564
00:59:23,595 --> 00:59:25,195
Didn't you hear it on the radio?

1565
00:59:25,195 --> 00:59:26,863
They found his body
behind drive-in.

1566
00:59:26,863 --> 00:59:28,398
He's dead.

1567
00:59:28,398 --> 00:59:30,167
- Okay, baby, just
try and relax.

1568
00:59:30,167 --> 00:59:31,335
- Relax?

1569
00:59:31,335 --> 00:59:32,370
Don't you understand?

1570
00:59:32,370 --> 00:59:33,638
We're next.

1571
00:59:33,638 --> 00:59:34,972
He's killed Peter
and Susie and Jim.

1572
00:59:34,972 --> 00:59:36,240
We're next.

1573
00:59:36,240 --> 00:59:38,242
- Do you think
you could go next?

1574
00:59:38,242 --> 00:59:39,510
- It's Amy, Ma.

1575
00:59:39,510 --> 00:59:41,712
- [Woman] Oh, well,
say hello for me, dear.

1576
00:59:41,712 --> 00:59:43,113
- [Bobby] My mother says hello.

1577
00:59:43,113 --> 00:59:44,215
- Are you crazy?

1578
00:59:44,215 --> 00:59:46,650
Don't you see that we're next?

1579
00:59:46,650 --> 00:59:47,718
- All right.

1580
00:59:47,718 --> 00:59:48,653
Where are you?

1581
00:59:48,653 --> 00:59:50,087
- [Tom] I'm, I'm here, I think.

1582
00:59:50,087 --> 00:59:51,188
- I'm at home.

1583
00:59:51,188 --> 00:59:52,723
- [Bobby] Is there anyone there?

1584
00:59:52,723 --> 00:59:53,557
- No.

1585
00:59:53,557 --> 00:59:54,392
- Uh, except for me.

1586
00:59:54,392 --> 00:59:55,225
- I'm alone.

1587
00:59:55,225 --> 00:59:56,060
My mother went to--

1588
00:59:56,060 --> 00:59:56,893
- Good.

1589
00:59:56,893 --> 00:59:58,128
Now listen.

1590
00:59:58,128 --> 00:59:59,063
Stay where you are,
I'm coming right over.

1591
00:59:59,063 --> 01:00:00,498
- [Mike] Small comfort, I know.

1592
01:00:00,498 --> 01:00:04,135
- Lock the doors and
don't let anyone in, okay?

1593
01:00:04,135 --> 01:00:04,935
- Okay.

1594
01:00:04,935 --> 01:00:06,070
- I'll be right there.

1595
01:00:06,070 --> 01:00:08,138
- But don't let me in.

1596
01:00:08,138 --> 01:00:09,507
- Don't worry.

1597
01:00:09,507 --> 01:00:11,675
Nothing's going to happen.

1598
01:00:15,078 --> 01:00:17,682
- [Mike] How did this get here?

1599
01:00:19,050 --> 01:00:21,385
- Whoa, check out the teddy.

1600
01:00:22,753 --> 01:00:24,555
- [Tom] We've taken the Sears
Auto Center waiting room

1601
01:00:24,555 --> 01:00:27,225
and turned it into headquarters.

1602
01:00:30,260 --> 01:00:33,330
- [Mike] Whoa, Stiff
Bater is pissed.

1603
01:00:34,765 --> 01:00:37,235
- Hey, you smashed my sandwich!

1604
01:00:37,235 --> 01:00:39,203
(grunting)

1605
01:00:39,203 --> 01:00:40,772
- [Tom] Does anybody
have their gun?

1606
01:00:40,772 --> 01:00:43,607
- Anybody got
handcuffs or anything?

1607
01:00:43,607 --> 01:00:46,043
(screaming)

1608
01:00:46,043 --> 01:00:49,280
Please, sir, just
pay the parking fine.

1609
01:00:50,615 --> 01:00:52,183
- [Tom] Boy, wait till
my Young Life meeting

1610
01:00:52,183 --> 01:00:53,952
hears about this.

1611
01:00:53,952 --> 01:00:55,587
- Take a good look, friend.

1612
01:00:55,587 --> 01:00:56,653
There's your killer.

1613
01:00:56,653 --> 01:00:57,522
- [Mike] Mine, sir?

1614
01:00:57,522 --> 01:00:58,790
You mean it?

1615
01:00:58,790 --> 01:01:01,525
(screaming)

1616
01:01:01,525 --> 01:01:04,062
- This scene was cut
from the program.

1617
01:01:04,062 --> 01:01:05,228
- [Mike] Tear gas, mace, anyone?

1618
01:01:05,228 --> 01:01:07,365
- James Earl Powell.

1619
01:01:07,365 --> 01:01:09,000
We picked him up in New Castle.

1620
01:01:09,000 --> 01:01:10,267
- He was bringing coals.

1621
01:01:10,267 --> 01:01:13,270
- He was trying to rob
a check cashing store.

1622
01:01:13,270 --> 01:01:15,740
James is a very bad boy.

1623
01:01:15,740 --> 01:01:17,608
He was on probation.

1624
01:01:17,608 --> 01:01:19,577
- Let me guess, assault.

1625
01:01:19,577 --> 01:01:20,712
- [Tom] No, a pepper.

1626
01:01:20,712 --> 01:01:21,545
Ha ha.

1627
01:01:21,545 --> 01:01:22,713
- Yeah, right.

1628
01:01:24,115 --> 01:01:27,718
Seems he likes to beat
up people and rob 'em.

1629
01:01:27,718 --> 01:01:28,987
You may have noticed.

1630
01:01:28,987 --> 01:01:30,388
- I'm Adam West.

1631
01:01:30,388 --> 01:01:34,058
- [Man] James is a
terrifyingly strong dude.

1632
01:01:34,058 --> 01:01:35,058
- [Tom] Dude, sir?

1633
01:01:35,058 --> 01:01:37,762
- Then why did he kill the kids?

1634
01:01:37,762 --> 01:01:39,197
Then why did he kill the kids?

1635
01:01:39,197 --> 01:01:40,498
You know none of
them were robbed.

1636
01:01:40,498 --> 01:01:41,998
- [Tom] Take two.

1637
01:01:41,998 --> 01:01:43,367
- I don't know, maybe he
was working for somebody,

1638
01:01:43,367 --> 01:01:45,670
maybe he's got a new hobby.

1639
01:01:45,670 --> 01:01:47,338
But we've got him now
and we'll find out

1640
01:01:47,338 --> 01:01:48,873
just as soon as he talks.

1641
01:01:48,873 --> 01:01:50,442
- [Mike] Now, Chief O'Hara, oh.

1642
01:01:50,442 --> 01:01:52,510
- What's the matter, Frank?

1643
01:01:52,510 --> 01:01:54,578
A little flesh wound
because you couldn't

1644
01:01:54,578 --> 01:01:56,613
solve this case yourself?

1645
01:01:57,715 --> 01:01:59,183
- I'll check the script.

1646
01:01:59,183 --> 01:02:02,320
- Look, the object is
to clear these cases

1647
01:02:02,320 --> 01:02:04,122
as soon as possible.

1648
01:02:04,122 --> 01:02:06,123
- Maybe too soon.

1649
01:02:06,123 --> 01:02:08,993
- You're trying to say
we got the wrong man?

1650
01:02:08,993 --> 01:02:13,230
- Look, I just don't think that
Mr. James there is our man.

1651
01:02:13,230 --> 01:02:14,698
- Do you have
somebody else in mind?

1652
01:02:14,698 --> 01:02:16,533
- [Tom] Well, my uncle's nice.

1653
01:02:16,533 --> 01:02:18,068
- It's just a
feeling, that's all.

1654
01:02:18,068 --> 01:02:20,572
- I just feel like crying.

1655
01:02:20,572 --> 01:02:21,405
- Oh, yes.

1656
01:02:23,340 --> 01:02:24,442
Feeling.

1657
01:02:24,442 --> 01:02:26,643
Must be that
policeman's intuition

1658
01:02:26,643 --> 01:02:30,413
you've developed after all
these years with the force.

1659
01:02:30,413 --> 01:02:31,982
Oh, come on, Frank.

1660
01:02:33,317 --> 01:02:35,052
You're just a little
ticked because you couldn't

1661
01:02:35,052 --> 01:02:39,723
grab the brass ring and
solve this case yourself.

1662
01:02:39,723 --> 01:02:41,858
Come on, you've got a
lot of years ahead of you

1663
01:02:41,858 --> 01:02:43,493
to blow cases.

1664
01:02:43,493 --> 01:02:45,195
Just be happy this one's solved.

1665
01:02:45,195 --> 01:02:46,030
- [Mike] Yeah, come on.

1666
01:02:46,030 --> 01:02:47,765
Where's that's smile?

1667
01:02:50,568 --> 01:02:51,535
- Come on, Frank.

1668
01:02:51,535 --> 01:02:52,270
- [Tom] No, not the belt!

1669
01:02:52,270 --> 01:02:53,103
- [Mike] No!

1670
01:02:53,103 --> 01:02:54,438
- I'll buy you a drink.

1671
01:02:54,438 --> 01:02:55,673
- It is 10 a.m.

1672
01:02:56,840 --> 01:02:59,477
- [Mike] Guy just got a timeout.

1673
01:03:00,578 --> 01:03:03,647
(upbeat synth music)

1674
01:03:08,318 --> 01:03:10,320
(grunting)

1675
01:03:10,320 --> 01:03:12,857
- [Tom] The word
truncheon springs to mind.

1676
01:03:12,857 --> 01:03:13,690
Cudgel.

1677
01:03:13,690 --> 01:03:14,525
- Bad boy.

1678
01:03:14,525 --> 01:03:15,458
- [Mike] Oh.

1679
01:03:15,458 --> 01:03:17,093
- Oh, that was easy for him.

1680
01:03:17,093 --> 01:03:19,430
He just pretended
it was Tim Burton.

1681
01:03:19,430 --> 01:03:21,532
- [Mike] Uh, that
didn't help much, sir.

1682
01:03:21,532 --> 01:03:23,400
Thanks anyway.

1683
01:03:23,400 --> 01:03:26,537
- [Tom] Auditions
for the band Fear.

1684
01:03:26,537 --> 01:03:28,338
- The three faces of Steve.

1685
01:03:28,338 --> 01:03:30,975
(screaming)

1686
01:03:30,975 --> 01:03:34,545
- Did you have to order
me a corn-god, sir.

1687
01:03:36,013 --> 01:03:37,482
- [Tom] Adam West did his
own stunts in this scene.

1688
01:03:37,482 --> 01:03:41,385
- [Mike] Could I get a
booster chair for my friend.

1689
01:03:41,385 --> 01:03:43,353
- Just need to be
treated with respect.

1690
01:03:43,353 --> 01:03:45,523
Could I get another
Shirley Temple, please.

1691
01:03:45,523 --> 01:03:48,358
- Well, here's to the
ones who got away.

1692
01:03:48,358 --> 01:03:50,360
- [Tom] Away, heh.

1693
01:03:50,360 --> 01:03:52,363
- Hope my pirate
meal has onion rings.

1694
01:03:52,363 --> 01:03:53,865
Take me away 7-Up.

1695
01:03:55,032 --> 01:03:58,402
- [Tom] This is
all too familiar.

1696
01:03:58,402 --> 01:04:00,738
- How long's it been, Frank?

1697
01:04:01,772 --> 01:04:02,740
- I don't know.

1698
01:04:02,740 --> 01:04:04,075
- You know me too well.

1699
01:04:04,075 --> 01:04:05,075
- Two years.

1700
01:04:06,243 --> 01:04:08,278
- Oh, you'll get over it.

1701
01:04:08,278 --> 01:04:12,383
Took me about two
centuries, but it'll work.

1702
01:04:12,383 --> 01:04:13,650
Hey.

1703
01:04:13,650 --> 01:04:15,787
Come on, this is a celebration.

1704
01:04:15,787 --> 01:04:17,288
The cases is closed.

1705
01:04:17,288 --> 01:04:18,188
- [Mike] Well, if
it's a celebration,

1706
01:04:18,188 --> 01:04:19,123
why are we at Chi Chi's?

1707
01:04:19,123 --> 01:04:20,592
- I know, I'm sorry.

1708
01:04:20,592 --> 01:04:22,693
- I can't do this before
breakfast, I'm not like you.

1709
01:04:22,693 --> 01:04:24,095
- You should have seen it.

1710
01:04:24,095 --> 01:04:26,730
I mean, this kid was
impaled with a baseball bat.

1711
01:04:26,730 --> 01:04:29,933
I just don't understand how
this guy James Earl could do it?

1712
01:04:29,933 --> 01:04:33,070
- Maybe James Earl has
a great batting average.

1713
01:04:33,070 --> 01:04:35,438
- [Tom] But it's the RBI's
that count, isn't it?

1714
01:04:35,438 --> 01:04:37,073
- Cap, this wasn't
like anything.

1715
01:04:37,073 --> 01:04:38,542
I mean, look at this kid.

1716
01:04:38,542 --> 01:04:40,477
He's got a baseball bat shoved
right through his stomach.

1717
01:04:40,477 --> 01:04:42,680
- Frank, I did not come here
to look at dirty pictures.

1718
01:04:42,680 --> 01:04:44,215
You take enough of
stuff home with you,

1719
01:04:44,215 --> 01:04:46,683
pretty soon there's not going
to be anything else at home.

1720
01:04:46,683 --> 01:04:49,353
- [Mike] And you got to
leave room for liquor.

1721
01:04:49,353 --> 01:04:50,187
- Hey!

1722
01:04:50,187 --> 01:04:51,088
- What?

1723
01:04:51,088 --> 01:04:52,757
- This is a celebration.

1724
01:04:52,757 --> 01:04:53,590
Hey!

1725
01:04:53,590 --> 01:04:55,425
Hey, the case is closed.

1726
01:04:55,425 --> 01:04:58,262
- [Tom] Long live the case!

1727
01:04:58,262 --> 01:04:59,597
- [Man] Hey!

1728
01:04:59,597 --> 01:05:00,497
- [Tom] Hey!

1729
01:05:00,497 --> 01:05:01,332
- [Mike] Hey!

1730
01:05:01,332 --> 01:05:02,198
- [Tom] Hey!

1731
01:05:02,198 --> 01:05:03,000
- Hey!

1732
01:05:03,000 --> 01:05:03,833
- [Mike] Hey!

1733
01:05:03,833 --> 01:05:04,668
- [Tom] Hey!

1734
01:05:04,668 --> 01:05:05,502
- [Mike] Hey!

1735
01:05:05,502 --> 01:05:06,337
- Hey

1736
01:05:06,337 --> 01:05:07,170
- [Tom] Hey!

1737
01:05:07,170 --> 01:05:08,005
- [Mike] Hey!

1738
01:05:08,005 --> 01:05:08,838
- Hey!

1739
01:05:08,838 --> 01:05:10,273
- [Tom] Hey!

1740
01:05:10,273 --> 01:05:11,108
Hey!

1741
01:05:11,108 --> 01:05:12,743
- Hey!

1742
01:05:12,743 --> 01:05:13,945
- [Mike] Hey!

1743
01:05:13,945 --> 01:05:15,713
- It's her first
zombie commissioned

1744
01:05:15,713 --> 01:05:17,882
in a couple of years, so
she's babysitting the case.

1745
01:05:17,882 --> 01:05:19,883
(roars)

1746
01:05:21,618 --> 01:05:23,887
- [Mike] Your mystery date.

1747
01:05:25,657 --> 01:05:27,525
- [Tom] It's five a.m.
and Mr. Zombie's day

1748
01:05:27,525 --> 01:05:29,527
is just beginning.

1749
01:05:29,527 --> 01:05:34,532
- [Mike] He's off for a
long day of job interviews.

1750
01:05:35,398 --> 01:05:36,333
- Uh, I've got to get a new bad.

1751
01:05:36,333 --> 01:05:38,168
Slept like crap again.

1752
01:05:39,237 --> 01:05:40,303
- [Tom] No, no, don't help me.

1753
01:05:40,303 --> 01:05:41,838
I've got it.

1754
01:05:41,838 --> 01:05:43,007
- [Mike] Watch my
casket, will you.

1755
01:05:43,007 --> 01:05:44,242
Don't drive it.

1756
01:05:45,677 --> 01:05:48,512
- Wow, he's really
last his looks.

1757
01:05:50,080 --> 01:05:51,282
- [Tom] Just once I'd
like to see a zombie

1758
01:05:51,282 --> 01:05:52,650
with a little more
get up and go.

1759
01:05:52,650 --> 01:05:53,517
- Eh.

1760
01:05:53,517 --> 01:05:55,653
(humming)

1761
01:05:57,253 --> 01:05:58,155
- [Tom] Don't.

1762
01:05:58,155 --> 01:05:59,390
- [Mike] Sorry.

1763
01:06:00,758 --> 01:06:03,293
- It went from a high rise
exterior to someone's basement.

1764
01:06:03,293 --> 01:06:06,297
- [Tom] Oh, he's hitting
the note pretty hard there.

1765
01:06:06,297 --> 01:06:07,498
- [Mike] If I had a girlfriend,

1766
01:06:07,498 --> 01:06:09,567
she'd be sitting right
there, right now.

1767
01:06:09,567 --> 01:06:11,802
- He needs to unify
his design concept.

1768
01:06:11,802 --> 01:06:14,238
- [Mike] Corduroy
chair's nice, though.

1769
01:06:14,238 --> 01:06:19,143
- [Tom] Mmm, self-bondage
really doesn't work out.

1770
01:06:19,143 --> 01:06:21,012
- [Frank] This
case isn't closed.

1771
01:06:21,012 --> 01:06:22,312
- [Mike] I just realized
something we're not

1772
01:06:22,312 --> 01:06:24,048
going to bother
showing the audience.

1773
01:06:24,048 --> 01:06:24,882
Ha!

1774
01:06:24,882 --> 01:06:26,117
(light synth music)

1775
01:06:26,117 --> 01:06:29,587
He's being stalked
by Depeche Mode.

1776
01:06:29,587 --> 01:06:31,488
(hums)

1777
01:06:33,590 --> 01:06:36,360
- [Tom] Johnson's
wedding got out of hand.

1778
01:06:36,360 --> 01:06:39,930
- [Mike] Remind me
