Hmm, sensible.

2037
01:14:48,685 --> 01:14:50,753
(birds chirping)

2038
01:14:50,753 --> 01:14:52,355
- This is Charlie 117, come in.

2039
01:14:52,355 --> 01:14:55,592
- [Tom] I've got birds, over.

2040
01:14:55,592 --> 01:14:56,427
- Oh, I knew it.

2041
01:14:56,427 --> 01:14:57,493
- [Tom] Shut up.

2042
01:14:57,493 --> 01:14:58,395
- I'll be right there.

2043
01:14:58,395 --> 01:14:59,362
- Water in the basement.

2044
01:14:59,362 --> 01:15:00,197
Darn it!

2045
01:15:02,765 --> 01:15:03,833
- [Mike] Your worst nightmare,

2046
01:15:03,833 --> 01:15:06,237
a cop with a learner's permit.

2047
01:15:06,237 --> 01:15:08,638
- [Tom] Hal Needham was brought
in to direct this scene.

2048
01:15:08,638 --> 01:15:09,807
(siren wailing)

2049
01:15:09,807 --> 01:15:11,040
And that's all.

2050
01:15:15,212 --> 01:15:20,083
- Oh, that's fine, we'll just
walk to the curb from here.

2051
01:15:20,083 --> 01:15:21,685
- [Man] You two, get
those people out of here.

2052
01:15:21,685 --> 01:15:23,220
- Oh, yeah, you can use it.

2053
01:15:23,220 --> 01:15:24,688
- Hi, Frank.

2054
01:15:24,688 --> 01:15:26,457
We've got another one
just like the last three.

2055
01:15:26,457 --> 01:15:27,290
- Neck broken?

2056
01:15:27,290 --> 01:15:28,158
- Yeah, like a twig.

2057
01:15:28,158 --> 01:15:29,225
- [Mike] Oh, nice image.

2058
01:15:29,225 --> 01:15:30,227
- How old is the kid?

2059
01:15:30,227 --> 01:15:31,828
- I'd say about 43.

2060
01:15:32,828 --> 01:15:34,163
- What, an old man?

2061
01:15:34,163 --> 01:15:34,998
- Yeah.

2062
01:15:34,998 --> 01:15:36,233
- Hey, thanks, Frank.

2063
01:15:36,233 --> 01:15:37,167
We can't all look
as young as you now.

2064
01:15:37,167 --> 01:15:38,902
- [Tom] Oh, great, he's back.

2065
01:15:38,902 --> 01:15:40,437
- Do you, uh, do
you think this could

2066
01:15:40,437 --> 01:15:42,338
have been done by the same
assailant as the others.

2067
01:15:42,338 --> 01:15:45,008
- I'd stake my semi-professional
reputation on it.

2068
01:15:45,008 --> 01:15:45,842
(laughs)

2069
01:15:45,842 --> 01:15:47,243
- [Tom] Stop.

2070
01:15:47,243 --> 01:15:48,845
- So, who is this guy?

2071
01:15:48,845 --> 01:15:51,748
- That's the kicker, he's
the last kid's father.

2072
01:15:51,748 --> 01:15:53,417
- [Tom] Father.

2073
01:15:53,417 --> 01:15:56,453
- Oh, I left my lights on again.

2074
01:15:56,453 --> 01:15:57,687
- [Man] Hey, Frank!

2075
01:15:57,687 --> 01:15:59,555
Don't you want to
check the house?

2076
01:15:59,555 --> 01:16:00,957
- I'm more interested
in the crowd.

2077
01:16:00,957 --> 01:16:02,358
- [Mike] I'm, uh, running
for state auditor.

2078
01:16:02,358 --> 01:16:03,160
Hi, folks!

2079
01:16:03,160 --> 01:16:04,293
Hi.

2080
01:16:04,293 --> 01:16:05,228
- Come on, Amy.

2081
01:16:05,228 --> 01:16:06,463
We'll buy you clothes when--

2082
01:16:06,463 --> 01:16:07,697
- [Tom] Oh, look, she
put her breasts on.

2083
01:16:07,697 --> 01:16:08,865
- Should I leave
a note for my mom?

2084
01:16:08,865 --> 01:16:10,333
- Ah, she'll just
think you got lost in--

2085
01:16:10,333 --> 01:16:14,437
- But should I bring my sports
bra in case I get chased?

2086
01:16:17,640 --> 01:16:21,278
- [Mike] This spot
reserved for Viper.

2087
01:16:21,278 --> 01:16:22,645
- [Tom] Guests being
stalked by zombies

2088
01:16:22,645 --> 01:16:24,848
stay at Best Western Hotel.

2089
01:16:27,717 --> 01:16:28,952
- See, no prob.

2090
01:16:30,387 --> 01:16:31,855
Mr. Key was right where
old Jim said it would be.

2091
01:16:31,855 --> 01:16:34,590
- [Tom] He's dressed for
ladies' night at Shenanigans.

2092
01:16:34,590 --> 01:16:35,558
- Yeah, well, we're not
going to end up like,

2093
01:16:35,558 --> 01:16:36,960
Jim, you hear me?

2094
01:16:38,395 --> 01:16:42,465
Let's just get this cash,
and then we're history.

2095
01:16:46,268 --> 01:16:47,270
- [Tom] Hey.

2096
01:16:48,505 --> 01:16:50,107
If Mr. Blackstone
was a zombie, he'd

2097
01:16:50,107 --> 01:16:51,708
kill her just for that skirt.

2098
01:16:51,708 --> 01:16:52,542
- Mmhmm.

2099
01:16:54,110 --> 01:16:55,478
- This is a big garage.

2100
01:16:55,478 --> 01:16:56,813
- [Mike] See, she's
not that dumb.

2101
01:16:56,813 --> 01:16:58,915
- Yeah, a little too big.

2102
01:17:00,983 --> 01:17:02,952
- I wonder where they
keep their money.

2103
01:17:02,952 --> 01:17:06,088
- Yeah, good question,
a little too good.

2104
01:17:06,088 --> 01:17:09,727
- [Tom] Oh, must you
superlative everything?

2105
01:17:09,727 --> 01:17:11,027
