ominous in here.

2106
01:17:11,027 --> 01:17:13,163
A little too ominous.

2107
01:17:13,163 --> 01:17:14,430
- A lot of cars in here.

2108
01:17:14,430 --> 01:17:15,732
- [Mike] A little too
a lot of cars in here.

2109
01:17:15,732 --> 01:17:17,833
- [Tom] Would you please.

2110
01:17:19,135 --> 01:17:22,938
A Francis Ford Coppola
production or a Kenneth Branagh

2111
01:17:22,938 --> 01:17:26,943
film Kera Cutley in Ali
Sheedy's "Frankenstein."

2112
01:17:34,685 --> 01:17:35,518
- [Mike] Tommy Lee Jones.

2113
01:17:35,518 --> 01:17:36,353
(roars)

2114
01:17:36,353 --> 01:17:37,187
- He's a great actor.

2115
01:17:37,187 --> 01:17:38,388
- [Mike] Yeah.

2116
01:17:38,388 --> 01:17:39,188
- We ain't ever going
to find this money

2117
01:17:39,188 --> 01:17:40,390
if we don't split up.

2118
01:17:40,390 --> 01:17:42,258
- [Tom] Are you
breaking up with me?

2119
01:17:42,258 --> 01:17:43,260
- I'm going to go
check over here.

2120
01:17:43,260 --> 01:17:44,260
You go check over there.

2121
01:17:44,260 --> 01:17:45,195
Just check around, okay?

2122
01:17:45,195 --> 01:17:46,430
- This place is creepy.

2123
01:17:46,430 --> 01:17:47,463
I don't want to go
there by myself.

2124
01:17:47,463 --> 01:17:49,432
- Just do as I told you, okay?

2125
01:17:49,432 --> 01:17:51,602
- [Tom] Check out
that dark corner.

2126
01:17:51,602 --> 01:17:52,435
- Go.

2127
01:17:52,435 --> 01:17:53,270
Go in.

2128
01:17:57,340 --> 01:17:59,408
♪ You spin me
right round, baby ♪

2129
01:17:59,408 --> 01:18:02,312
♪ Right round like
a record, baby ♪

2130
01:18:02,312 --> 01:18:03,280
Remember that song?

2131
01:18:03,280 --> 01:18:05,015
- [Tom] No.

2132
01:18:05,015 --> 01:18:08,685
I thought she was being
followed by Al Gore.

2133
01:18:11,087 --> 01:18:13,090
- Why's he crab-walking?

2134
01:18:21,432 --> 01:18:23,100
- [Mike] Hey, is
my Buick ready yet?

2135
01:18:23,100 --> 01:18:24,300
- [Tom] Hello!

2136
01:18:24,300 --> 01:18:26,135
Is there a salesman
who can help me?

2137
01:18:26,135 --> 01:18:27,403
(growls)

2138
01:18:27,403 --> 01:18:28,338
- Boy, the zombie's got to clear

2139
01:18:28,338 --> 01:18:29,740
that frog out of his throat.

2140
01:18:29,740 --> 01:18:30,940
(coughs)

2141
01:18:30,940 --> 01:18:35,045
- [Mike] He sounds
like Harvey Fierstein.

2142
01:18:35,045 --> 01:18:36,680
- [Tom] Oh, he's balding, look.

2143
01:18:36,680 --> 01:18:37,980
- Oh, so does that
mean his grandfather

2144
01:18:37,980 --> 01:18:41,485
on his mother's side
was a balding zombie?

2145
01:18:46,790 --> 01:18:49,692
- [Mike] Where are those
commemorative place mats?

2146
01:18:49,692 --> 01:18:50,860
Stupid garage.

2147
01:18:52,395 --> 01:18:56,232
- [Tom] That's clearly
not the original actor.

2148
01:18:57,300 --> 01:18:58,135
- [Mike] Hi.

2149
01:18:58,135 --> 01:19:00,070
What can I do you for?

2150
01:19:00,070 --> 01:19:01,003
- [Tom] Wow!

2151
01:19:01,003 --> 01:19:04,107
(upbeat synth music)

2152
01:19:11,848 --> 01:19:12,748
- [Mike] Howdy.

2153
01:19:12,748 --> 01:19:14,750
That your zombie, ma'am?

2154
01:19:19,222 --> 01:19:21,023
- [Tom] Stop that.

2155
01:19:21,023 --> 01:19:21,958
Let me move my bike.

2156
01:19:21,958 --> 01:19:22,792
Hang on.

2157
01:19:26,463 --> 01:19:31,133
- [Mike] That's a really
trivial use of her dark powers.

2158
01:19:33,737 --> 01:19:34,570
(screams)

2159
01:19:34,570 --> 01:19:36,105
- [Tom] Cut, cut.

2160
01:19:36,105 --> 01:19:38,575
Tia, you're supposed to be in
your underwear in this scene.

2161
01:19:38,575 --> 01:19:41,443
(screams)

2162
01:19:41,443 --> 01:19:42,278
- No!

2163
01:19:42,278 --> 01:19:44,447
♪ Start spreading news ♪

2164
01:19:44,447 --> 01:19:45,882
(screams)

2165
01:19:45,882 --> 01:19:47,250
- [Mike] Well, Tia,
it's still better

2166
01:19:47,250 --> 01:19:49,518
than working with Mike Myers.

2167
01:19:49,518 --> 01:19:50,353
(growls)

2168
01:19:50,353 --> 01:19:51,522
- [Tom] Excuse me, miss.

2169
01:19:51,522 --> 01:19:54,290
That's for authorized
personnel only.

2170
01:19:55,558 --> 01:19:56,827
- [Mike] This is a big garage.

2171
01:19:56,827 --> 01:19:59,228
- Yeah, it's even
got a subway stop.

2172
01:19:59,228 --> 01:20:00,763
(growls)

2173
01:20:00,763 --> 01:20:04,200
♪ Some enchanted evening ♪

2174
01:20:08,172 --> 01:20:10,573
- [Mike] How'd he do that?

2175
01:20:10,573 --> 01:20:11,742
- [Tom] He's a pro.

2176
01:20:11,742 --> 01:20:14,743
- [Mike] She's hiding
behind a window!

2177
01:20:16,880 --> 01:20:17,780
- [Tom] Oh.

2178
01:20:21,150 --> 01:20:22,985
Oh, that one's got a
way with zombies, huh?

2179
01:20:22,985 --> 01:20:23,820
- [Mike] Mm-hmm.

2180
01:20:23,820 --> 01:20:25,822
(grunting)

2181
01:20:25,822 --> 01:20:26,757
- Oh!

2182
01:20:26,757 --> 01:20:28,825
Right on his luggage rack!

2183
01:20:30,260 --> 01:20:32,095
- [Mike] Admittedly, that's
an aggressive sales technique,

2184
01:20:32,095 --> 01:20:33,363
but, you know.

2185
01:20:33,363 --> 01:20:34,697
- [Tom] You're right,
paint job looks fine.

2186
01:20:34,697 --> 01:20:35,532
Sorry I complained.

2187
01:20:35,532 --> 01:20:36,365
Ba-bye.

2188
01:20:37,333 --> 01:20:38,502
- That was great.

2189
01:20:38,502 --> 01:20:41,905
I've never been handled
like that before.

2190
01:20:43,138 --> 01:20:45,942
- [Mike] This is a
really big garage.

2191
01:20:48,745 --> 01:20:50,080
- [Tom] Shari
Belafonte in "Harper."

2192
01:20:50,080 --> 01:20:52,382
- Well, looky here.

2193
01:20:52,382 --> 01:20:53,950
- How you diddly doing?

2194
01:20:53,950 --> 01:20:56,018
- Aren't you in the wrong
neighborhood little girl?

2195
01:20:56,018 --> 01:20:57,420
- [Mike] I'm Batman.

2196
01:20:57,420 --> 01:20:59,222
- Looks like I missed
the start of the party.

2197
01:20:59,222 --> 01:21:02,225
Why don't you show me
where the guests are going.

2198
01:21:02,225 --> 01:21:04,393
Get in the car, witch.

2199
01:21:04,393 --> 01:21:06,128
- Yes, Mr. Churchman.

2200
01:21:07,297 --> 01:21:08,898
- [Tom] Oh, is your
Batmobile in the shop?

2201
01:21:08,898 --> 01:21:10,767
- [Mike] Shut up.

2202
01:21:10,767 --> 01:21:14,670
(ominous synth music)

2203
01:21:14,670 --> 01:21:17,173
♪ Her name is Rio and she-- ♪

2204
01:21:17,173 --> 01:21:18,040
- [Mike] No.

2205
01:21:18,040 --> 01:21:19,608
No, never.

2206
01:21:19,608 --> 01:21:21,945
Look, it's Dondi the zombie.

2207
01:21:24,247 --> 01:21:26,315
- The zombie is deep in
the rough on the 13th.

2208
01:21:26,315 --> 01:21:29,718
He's got to put this
shot up to par the hole.

2209
01:21:29,718 --> 01:21:31,220
- [Mike] The hell is my grave?

2210
01:21:31,220 --> 01:21:35,225
Last time I crawled into the
wrong one, it was a mess.

2211
01:21:35,225 --> 01:21:36,492
- [Tom] You know,
ironically, they end up

2212
01:21:36,492 --> 01:21:39,395
busting the Zombie
for task evasion.

2213
01:21:41,898 --> 01:21:44,968
- Hey, uh, can I
have my thorax back?

2214
01:21:46,468 --> 01:21:47,970
- [Mike] Mr. Zombie,
I, I just need you

2215
01:21:47,970 --> 01:21:49,338
to sign this deposition.

2216
01:21:49,338 --> 01:21:51,140
It'll just take a sec.

2217
01:21:53,343 --> 01:21:58,315
♪ What would you sing
if I sang out of tune ♪

2218
01:21:59,248 --> 01:22:01,718
♪ Instead of what I mean ♪

2219
01:22:01,718 --> 01:22:03,387
He's choking up.

2220
01:22:03,387 --> 01:22:04,387
- Boy, I'm dead on my feet.

2221
01:22:04,387 --> 01:22:05,222
He he.

2222
01:22:05,222 --> 01:22:06,388
Dead, oh well.

2223
01:22:09,625 --> 01:22:12,862
- [Mike] It's doing
the nasty plunge.

2224
01:22:12,862 --> 01:22:13,730
Thud.

2225
01:22:18,267 --> 01:22:20,370
- [Tom] I mean, what's he, ew,

2226
01:22:20,370 --> 01:22:22,172
he's giving himself
a tongue bath.

2227
01:22:22,172 --> 01:22:23,005
Ew!

2228
01:22:24,007 --> 01:22:25,808
- Don't be afraid, Frank.

2229
01:22:25,808 --> 01:22:27,343
He won't bite you.

2230
01:22:27,343 --> 01:22:29,545
- [Mike] He might snap your
neck, but he won't bite you.

2231
01:22:29,545 --> 01:22:30,480
- Cap?

2232
01:22:30,480 --> 01:22:31,748
- [Mike] Aren't you Adam West

2233
01:22:31,748 --> 01:22:33,783
from "Lady
Chatterley's Lover 2"?

2234
01:22:33,783 --> 01:22:35,452
- The voodoo woman explained it

2235
01:22:35,452 --> 01:22:36,987
to me on the way over, Frank.

2236
01:22:36,987 --> 01:22:40,090
She made this kid a zombie
so it would avenge itself

2237
01:22:40,090 --> 01:22:43,960
against its murderers,
and avenge her against me.

2238
01:22:43,960 --> 01:22:45,128
- Oh!

2239
01:22:45,128 --> 01:22:46,395
- Against you?

2240
01:22:46,395 --> 01:22:49,398
- It's a long, sad
old story, Frank--

2241
01:22:49,398 --> 01:22:50,633
- [Tom] Yeah, I'll say.

2242
01:22:50,633 --> 01:22:52,168
- From before I
was on the force.

2243
01:22:52,168 --> 01:22:53,870
- [Tom] I had this
great cave, you see.

2244
01:22:53,870 --> 01:22:55,605
- A really sad story.

2245
01:22:57,073 --> 01:23:01,477
- He killed this boy's father
for trying to save my life.

2246
01:23:02,178 --> 01:23:02,978
- Is that true?

2247
01:23:02,978 --> 01:23:04,113
- That's true, Frank.

2248
01:23:04,113 --> 01:23:04,947
- Oh.

2249
01:23:06,082 --> 01:23:07,850
- But you see, zombies
lose their energy

2250
01:23:07,850 --> 01:23:10,453
after they revenge themselves.

2251
01:23:10,453 --> 01:23:14,690
So there'll be nobody around
to revenge old Molly Makembe.

2252
01:23:14,690 --> 01:23:15,992
- Oops.

2253
01:23:15,992 --> 01:23:18,293
- This case is closed, Frank.

2254
01:23:18,293 --> 01:23:19,128
(gun firing)

2255
01:23:19,128 --> 01:23:19,962
- [Tom] Oh!

2256
01:23:19,962 --> 01:23:21,197
Oh, wow.

2257
01:23:21,197 --> 01:23:21,932
Probably should have
seen that coming.

2258
01:23:21,932 --> 01:23:24,000
(growls)

2259
01:23:25,768 --> 01:23:28,237
- Oh, ah, there's one
spot I just can't do.

2260
01:23:28,237 --> 01:23:33,242
- This is the last evil you
will do on earth, Mr. Churchman.

2261
01:23:34,443 --> 01:23:35,678
- I think she's
going for some sort

2262
01:23:35,678 --> 01:23:38,180
of Elvis Patois kind of thing.

2263
01:23:38,180 --> 01:23:40,283
(growls)

2264
01:23:41,450 --> 01:23:42,752
